<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">mark</ansi>

Mark the things you never want to carry away from a merchant, then sell
them all at once.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">mark [item] junk</ansi>
  Marks an item you carry as junk. It shows a <ansi fg="item-flags">j</ansi> flag in your pack.

  <ansi fg="command">mark [item] keep</ansi>
  Takes the mark off again.

  <ansi fg="command">mark</ansi>
  Lists what you have marked.

  <ansi fg="command">sell junk</ansi>
  At a merchant, sells everything marked, plus plain junk-type items, in one
  transaction with one summary line per item. Any item no merchant here
  wants stays in your pack. A marked item is sold at the usual price, so
  mark gear you are done with, not gear you might still wear.

Quest items cannot be marked. The mark stays on an item when you hand it
to a companion, stash it or store it.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help sell</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help salvage</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help goods</ansi>.
